## Elasticsearch Aggregations

**What are Aggregations?**

Process of summarizing/grouping data (like SQL GROUP BY)

**Types:**

### 1. Metric Aggregations (Single Value)
```json
{
  "aggs": {
    "total_events": {
      "value_count": {
        "field": "event.id"
      }
    },
    "average_response_time": {
      "avg": {
        "field": "response.time"
      }
    },
    "max_bytes": {
      "max": {
        "field": "bytes"
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Returns: Single numbers (sum, average, max, min, etc.)

### 2. Bucket Aggregations (Group Data)
```json
{
  "aggs": {
    "events_by_user": {
      "terms": {
        "field": "user.name.keyword",
        "size": 10,
        "order": {"_count": "desc"}
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Returns:
```
user          | count
admin         | 1,245
john.smith    | 892
jane.doe      | 756
...
```

### 3. Nested Aggregations (Sub-groups)
```json
{
  "aggs": {
    "by_user": {
      "terms": {
        "field": "user.name.keyword"
      },
      "aggs": {
        "failure_count": {
          "value_count": {"field": "event.id"}
        },
        "source_ips": {
          "terms": {
            "field": "source.ip.keyword"
          }
        },
        "first_failure": {
          "min": {"field": "@timestamp"}
        },
        "last_failure": {
          "max": {"field": "@timestamp"}
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Returns comprehensive analysis:
```
user       | count | first_failure    | last_failure     | source_ips
admin      | 245   | 2025-12-31T01:00 | 2025-12-31T02:15 | [192.168.1.1, 192.168.1.2]
john.smith | 892   | 2025-12-31T00:15 | 2025-12-31T05:30 | [203.0.113.1, 203.0.113.2]
```

