**Q8: Compare query performance: Term vs. Match vs. Range queries. When use each?**

Answer:

| Query Type | Performance | Use Case | Example |
|-----------|------------|----------|---------|
| **Term** | FASTEST | Exact matches on keywords | `event.code: 4625` |
| **Range** | FAST | Numeric/date comparisons | `bytes > 1GB` |
| **Match** | SLOWER | Full-text search | Message contains "malware" |
| **Bool** | VARIES | Complex logic | Combined criteria |
| **Filter** | FASTEST (cached) | Boolean checks | Don't affect scoring |

Optimization Rules:
```
GOOD (Fast):
{
  "query": {
    "bool": {
      "must": [{"match": {"message": "error"}}],
      "filter": [{"range": {"@timestamp": {...}}},
                 {"term": {"host.os": "windows"}}]
    }
  }
}

BAD (Slow):
{
  "query": {
    "bool": {
      "must": [{"match": {"message": "error"}},
               {"range": {"@timestamp": {...}}},
               {"match": {"host.os": "windows"}}]
    }
  }
}

Difference: Filters don't calculate scores (2-3x faster)
```

