**Q9: Explain Index Lifecycle Management (ILM) and its cost benefits.**

Answer:

ILM moves indices through phases based on age:

```
Days 1-7: HOT Phase
├─ Storage: SSD (fastest, expensive)
├─ Replicas: 1 (full copies)
├─ Use Case: Recent incidents (most searched)
├─ Size: 7 days × 100GB = 700GB
├─ With replicas: 1,400GB
└─ Cost: $1,400/month @ $10/GB/month

    ↓ Auto-transition ↓

Days 8-60: WARM Phase
├─ Storage: HDD (slower, cheaper)
├─ Action: Shrink index (reduce shards 5→1)
├─ Replicas: 0 (reduced)
├─ Use Case: Historical search (less frequent)
├─ Size: ~500GB
└─ Cost: $250/month @ $5/GB/month

    ↓ Auto-transition ↓

Days 61+: COLD Phase
├─ Storage: Archive (slowest, cheapest)
├─ Action: Freeze index (read-only)
├─ Use Case: Compliance/audit (rarely searched)
├─ Size: ~500GB
└─ Cost: $50/month @ $1/GB/month

Total Annual Cost:
└─ Traditional (all HOT): 73TB × $10 = $876,000/year
└─ With ILM: $1,650/year
└─ SAVINGS: 99.8% 🎉
```

