## Elastic Best Practices

### Performance Optimization

```
1. INDEX TUNING
   - Set appropriate shard count (not too many)
   - Use proper replica count (usually 1)
   - Implement ILM for retention
   - Delete old indices instead of purging

2. QUERY OPTIMIZATION
   - Use filters instead of queries (faster)
   - Use term query, not match (when possible)
   - Limit time range (latest 7 days, not all time)
   - Use aggregation instead of sorting

3. HARDWARE ALLOCATION
   Master Nodes: 1GB heap minimum
   Data Nodes: 16-32GB heap (50% of system RAM max)
   Rule: Never set >50% system RAM as heap
   
4. STORAGE
   - SSD for HOT data (recent)
   - HDD for WARM data (30-90 days)
   - Archive for COLD data (>90 days)
```

### Security Best Practices

```
1. ACCESS CONTROL
   - Enable X-Pack Security
   - Use role-based access control (RBAC)
   - Restrict index access by role
   - Audit all authentication attempts

2. DATA PROTECTION
   - TLS/SSL encryption in transit
   - Encryption at rest (AES-256)
   - Regular backups (daily)
   - Test recovery procedures (monthly)

3. MONITORING
   - Monitor cluster health (green/yellow/red)
   - Alert on node failures
   - Track disk space usage
   - Monitor query performance
   - Review security logs monthly
```

